maluos-system-monitor (49.1+maluos.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13, shared GPUs, slice G5 (the local half): the MaluOS Network
    tab (this node as the gateway's node API reports it: name and id, the
    listener, sharing, the manager, the lanes, the keys issued; the nodes
    paired by hand; the office, with the estate's directory to follow) and
    the Queue tab (every lane with Pause/Resume, every queued or running
    call of every principal with Cancel and its class as a drop-down, live
    every two seconds through the session service's NodeQueue; the actions
    run maluctl gateway node …; "Open in Sovereign LLM Manager" when the
    desk is enrolled). Alt+5, Alt+6, --show-network-tab, --show-queue-tab.
  * One session client (maluos-session.cpp) shared by the three tabs: it
    polls GetState while a tab that draws the state is current and
    NodeQueue while the Queue tab is; the GPUs tab is rewritten on it. The
    self-test exercises the three tabs and prints one line:
    "self-test ok: GPUs: …; Network: …; Queue: …".

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0000

maluos-system-monitor (49.1+maluos.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The self-test no longer fails while a GetState call is still in flight:
    on a slow machine (the boot test under TCG) the window's first paint held
    the main loop past the 20 s deadline and the timer fired before the
    reply was dispatched. The deadline is now 60 s, a pending call is always
    waited for (the call's own 30 s timeout ends it), a refused call fails
    the test at once, and the FAIL line carries the D-Bus error.
  * The gsettings schema accepts `gpus` for current-tab, so the GPUs tab is
    remembered like the others (no "outside of valid range" warning).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000

